IMPORT `ccc-core`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-interpretation`
IMPORT `ccc20-part16-reverse-onus`

-- ccc20-part16-failure-and-delay.l4 -- sections 523.1 to 526 of the Criminal Code (Canada): the judicial referral hearing for a failure to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order
-- (s 523.1), the hearing on a contravention or a new offence while subject to one (s 524), the review of detention where the trial is delayed (s 525, the 90 days) and directions for expediting (s 526).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: a plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30); not the official text; nothing is claimed verified against the official text.
-- An answer is JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE (the text says no in its own words); NOTHING (not covered). A "may" whose "if" gate fails answers NOTHING (ruling of 2026-11-12); a duty and a bar answer JUST FALSE when their gate fails.
-- Offences named by section number are asked as the answer of the part that owns them: `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` (MAYBE BOOLEAN, carried through, never turned into FALSE).
-- The 90 days of section 525 are counted with `Date to days`: the day of the event is day 0 and the 90 days expire at the end of day 90 (fork F-90-days, the same count as the 30 days of ss 520(8) and 521(9)).

§ `Section 523.1 -- Judicial referral hearing for a failure to comply`

-- 523.1 (1) "When an accused appears before a justice in any of the circumstances described in subsection (2), the justice shall (a) if the accused was released from custody under an order made under
-- subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province, order that the accused appear before a judge of that court ...; or (b) in any other case, hear the matter."
-- The circumstances of (2) are a closed list ("are the following"), whose answer never is NOTHING, so the caller passes `s 523.1(2) ... EQUALS JUST TRUE` as a BOOLEAN.
-- src:11669 | 523.1 (1) When an accused appears before a justice in any of the circumstances described in subsection (2), the justice shall
-- src:11670 | (a) if the accused was released from custody under an order made under subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province, order that the accused appear before a judge of that court so that the judge may hear the matter; or
-- src:11671 | (b) in any other case, hear the matter.
@ref s 523.1(1) (src:11669-11671)
GIVEN `the circumstances described in subsection (2) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was released from custody under an order made under subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(1)(a) the justice must order that the accused appear before a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction so that the judge may hear the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the circumstances described in subsection (2) exist` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an accused appears before a justice in any of the circumstances described in subsection (2), the justice shall"
        IF `the accused was released from custody under an order made under subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the accused was released from custody under an order made under subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province" (in any other case paragraph (b) governs)

@ref s 523.1(1)(b) (src:11671)
GIVEN `the circumstances described in subsection (2) exist` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was released from custody under an order made under subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(1)(b) the justice must hear the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the circumstances described in subsection (2) exist` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "When an accused appears before a justice in any of the circumstances described in subsection (2), the justice shall"
        IF `the accused was released from custody under an order made under subsection 522(3) by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of any province` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case, hear the matter" (paragraph (a) governs this case)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- 523.1 (2) "The circumstances referred to in subsection (1) are the following: (a) an appearance notice has been issued to the accused for failing to comply with a summons, appearance notice,
-- undertaking or release order or to attend court as required and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section; or (b) a charge has been laid against the accused for the contravention referred to
-- in paragraph (a) and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section." "are the following" is read as closing the list (fork F-are-the-following).
-- src:11673 | (2) The circumstances referred to in subsection (1) are the following:
-- src:11674 | (a) an appearance notice has been issued to the accused for failing to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section; or
-- src:11675 | (b) a charge has been laid against the accused for the contravention referred to in paragraph (a) and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section.
@ref s 523.1(2) (src:11673-11675)
GIVEN `an appearance notice has been issued to the accused for failing to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(2)(a) an appearance notice has been issued for the failure and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section` MEANS
    IF `an appearance notice has been issued to the accused for failing to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required` AND `the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) an appearance notice has been issued to the accused for failing to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section"

@ref s 523.1(2)(b) (src:11675)
GIVEN `a charge has been laid against the accused for the contravention referred to in paragraph (a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(2)(b) a charge has been laid for the contravention and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section` MEANS
    IF `a charge has been laid against the accused for the contravention referred to in paragraph (a)` AND `the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) a charge has been laid against the accused for the contravention referred to in paragraph (a) and the prosecutor seeks a decision under this section"

@ref s 523.1(2) (src:11673-11675)
GIVEN `the answer of paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the answer of paragraph (b)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(2) the circumstances referred to in subsection (1) exist` MEANS
    IF `the answer of paragraph (a)` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `the answer of paragraph (b)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The circumstances referred to in subsection (1) are the following" (neither paragraph (a) nor paragraph (b) holds)

-- 523.1 (3) "If the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required and
-- that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss, the judge or justice shall review any conditions of release that have been imposed on the accused and may,
-- as the case may be, (a) take no action; (b) cancel any other summons ... and, as the case may be, (i) make a release order under section 515, or (ii) if the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of
-- the accused in custody is justified under subsection 515(10), make an order that the accused be detained in custody ...; or (c) remand the accused to custody for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act."
-- src:11677 | (3) If the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required and that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss, the judge or justice shall review any conditions of release that have been imposed on the accused and may, as the case may be,
-- src:11678 | (a) take no action;
-- src:11679 | (b) cancel any other summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order in respect of the accused and, as the case may be,
-- src:11680 | (i) make a release order under section 515, or
-- src:11681 | (ii) if the prosecutor shows cause why the detention of the accused in custody is justified under subsection 515(10), make an order that the accused be detained in custody until the accused is dealt with according to law and if so detained, the judge or justice shall include in the record a statement of the judge’s or justice’s reasons for making the order; or
-- src:11682 | (c) remand the accused to custody for the purposes of the Identification of Criminals Act.
@ref s 523.1(3) (src:11677-11682)
GIVEN `the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is satisfied that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(3) the judge or justice must review any conditions of release that have been imposed on the accused` MEANS
    IF `the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required`
        AND `the judge or justice is satisfied that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply ... and that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss, the judge or justice shall review any conditions of release"

@ref s 523.1(3)(a) (src:11678)
GIVEN `the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is satisfied that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(3)(a) the judge or justice may take no action` MEANS
    IF `the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required`
        AND `the judge or justice is satisfied that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge or justice ... is satisfied that ..., the judge or justice shall review any conditions of release ... and may, as the case may be, (a) take no action" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

