    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the judge or justice ... is satisfied that ..., ... may, as the case may be, ... (b) cancel any other summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order in respect of the accused" (a "may" whose "if" gate fails; the other reading is JUST FALSE)

@ref s 523.1(3)(b)(i) (src:11680)
GIVEN `the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice is satisfied that the failure did not cause a victim physical or emotional harm, property damage or economic loss` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge or justice cancels any other summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order in respect of the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 523.1(3)(b)(i) the judge or justice may make a release order under section 515` MEANS
    IF `the judge or justice who hears the matter is satisfied that the accused failed to comply with a summons, appearance notice, undertaking or release order or to attend court as required`
