§ `Section 525 -- Review of detention where the trial is delayed`

-- 525 (1) "The person having the custody of an accused -- who has been charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, who is being detained in custody pending their trial for that
-- offence and who is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter -- shall apply to a judge having jurisdiction in the place in which the accused is in custody to fix a date for a
-- hearing ..., if the trial has not commenced within 90 days from (a) the day on which the accused was taken before a justice under section 503; or (b) in the case where an order that the accused be detained
-- in custody has been made under section 521, paragraph 523.1(3)(b)(ii) or section 524, or a decision has been made with respect to a review under section 520, the later of the day on which the accused was taken
-- into custody under that order and the day of the decision. The person shall make the application immediately after the expiry of those 90 days."
-- The day the 90 days run from: (a) the day taken before a justice under s 503, unless (b)'s case exists, when it is the later of the two days (fork F-525-1-ab: the other reading counts from (a) as well).
-- src:11725 | 525 (1) The person having the custody of an accused — who has been charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469, who is being detained in custody pending their trial for that offence and who is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter — shall apply to a judge having jurisdiction in the place in which the accused is in custody to fix a date for a hearing to determine whether or not the accused should be released from custody, if the trial has not commenced within 90 days from
-- src:11726 | (a) the day on which the accused was taken before a justice under section 503; or
-- src:11727 | (b) in the case where an order that the accused be detained in custody has been made under section 521, paragraph 523.1(3)(b)(ii) or section 524, or a decision has been made with respect to a review under section 520, the later of the day on which the accused was taken into custody under that order and the day of the decision.
-- src:11728 | The person shall make the application immediately after the expiry of those 90 days.
@ref s 525(1) (src:11725-11728)
GIVEN `the day on which the accused was taken before a justice under section 503` IS A DATE
      `an order that the accused be detained in custody has been made under section 521, paragraph 523.1(3)(b)(ii) or section 524, or a decision has been made with respect to a review under section 520` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the accused was taken into custody under that order` IS A DATE
      `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 525(1) the day from which the 90 days are counted` MEANS
    IF `an order that the accused be detained in custody has been made under section 521, paragraph 523.1(3)(b)(ii) or section 524, or a decision has been made with respect to a review under section 520`
    THEN (IF `Date to days` `the day on which the accused was taken into custody under that order` AT LEAST `Date to days` `the day of the decision`
          THEN `the day on which the accused was taken into custody under that order`
          ELSE `the day of the decision`)
    ELSE `the day on which the accused was taken before a justice under section 503`

@ref s 525(1) the 90 days (src:11725)
GIVEN `the day from which the 90 days are counted` IS A DATE
      `the trial has commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day on which the trial commenced` IS A DATE
      `the day in question` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 525(1) the trial has not commenced within 90 days from the day` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the trial has commenced` AND `Date to days` `the day on which the trial commenced` MINUS `Date to days` `the day from which the 90 days are counted` AT MOST 90
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trial has not commenced within 90 days from" (the trial commenced within the 90 days)
        IF `Date to days` `the day in question` MINUS `Date to days` `the day from which the 90 days are counted` GREATER THAN 90 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trial has not commenced within 90 days from" (the 90 days have not yet expired: the condition is not yet met)

@ref s 525(1) the duty (src:11725-11728)
GIVEN `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the accused is being detained in custody pending their trial for that offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused is required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the trial has not commenced within 90 days` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused must apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the accused is being detained in custody pending their trial for that offence` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who is being detained in custody pending their trial for that offence"
        IF `the accused is required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who is not required to be detained in custody in respect of any other matter"
        IF NOT `the trial has not commenced within 90 days` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the trial has not commenced within 90 days from"
        IF `the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application if the accused has waived in writing their right to a hearing"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "who has been charged with an offence other than an offence listed in section 469"
        IF `s 469 the offence charged is one listed in section 469` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "an offence other than an offence listed in section 469" (section 469 is outside this range)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The time of the application: "The person shall make the application immediately after the expiry of those 90 days." "Immediately" has no counting rule in the text: the caller says whether the application was immediate.
@ref s 525(1) the time of the application (src:11728)
GIVEN `the day from which the 90 days are counted` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the application was made immediately after the expiry of the 90 days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 525(1) the application is made immediately after the expiry of those 90 days` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Date to days` `the day on which the application was made` MINUS `Date to days` `the day from which the 90 days are counted` AT MOST 90
            THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "immediately after the expiry of those 90 days" (the application was made before the 90 days expired)
        IF `the application was made immediately after the expiry of the 90 days` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The person shall make the application immediately after the expiry of those 90 days"

-- The duty as a regulative rule. The text names the actor only as "the person having the custody of an accused" and gives a time ("immediately after the expiry of those 90 days") but no count of days and no
-- consequence, so the rule has no WITHIN and no LEST. (The core's Party has no such actor: a local type, recorded in NEEDS-CORE.md.)
@ref s 525(1) the duty as a regulative rule (src:11728)
DECLARE `s 525(1) the actor` IS ONE OF
    `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused`

DECLARE `s 525(1) the act` IS ONE OF
    `s 525(1) apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing`

@ref s 525(1) the duty as a regulative rule (src:11725-11728)
GIVEN `the answer of s 525(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `s 525(1) the actor` `s 525(1) the act`
`s 525(1) the duty to apply` MEANS
    IF `the answer of s 525(1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN PARTY `s 525(1) the person having the custody of the accused`
         MUST `s 525(1) apply to a judge to fix a date for a hearing`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 525 (1.1) "However, the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application if the accused has waived in writing their right to a hearing and the judge has received the waiver
-- before the expiry of the 90-day period referred to in subsection (1)."
-- src:11730 | (1.1) However, the person having the custody of the accused is not required to make the application if the accused has waived in writing their right to a hearing and the judge has received the waiver before the expiry of the 90-day period referred to in subsection (1).
