    IF section's section EQUALS 495.1 OR section's section EQUALS 512.3 OR (section's section AT LEAST 517 AND section's section AT MOST 519) OR section's section EQUALS 524
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Sections 495.1, 512.3, 517 to 519 and 524 apply" (the text does not say "only"; another section is not covered)

-- 525 (7) "In this section, judge, in the Province of Quebec, (a) in the case where the order that the accused be detained in custody has been made by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of
-- the Province of Quebec, has the same meaning as in paragraph (b) of the definition judge in section 493; and (b) in any other case, means a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province,
-- a judge of the Court of Quebec or three judges of the Court of Quebec."
-- src:11754 | (7) In this section, judge, in the Province of Quebec,
-- src:11755 | (a) in the case where the order that the accused be detained in custody has been made by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province of Quebec, has the same meaning as in paragraph (b) of the definition judge in section 493; and
-- src:11756 | (b) in any other case, means a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province, a judge of the Court of Quebec or three judges of the Court of Quebec.
@ref s 525(7) (src:11754-11756)
DECLARE `s 525(7) the office the person holds` IS ONE OF
    `s 525(7) a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province`
    `s 525(7) a judge of the Court of Quebec`
    `s 525(7) three judges of the Court of Quebec`
    `s 525(7) an office that is none of those`

@ref s 525(7) the mapping to the offices of section 493 (src:11755)
GIVEN office IS A `s 525(7) the office the person holds`
GIVETH A `s 493 the office the person holds`
`s 525(7)(a) the office as section 493 knows it` MEANS
    CONSIDER office
    WHEN `s 525(7) a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province` THEN `s 493 a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province`
    WHEN `s 525(7) a judge of the Court of Quebec` THEN `s 493 an office that is none of those`
    WHEN `s 525(7) three judges of the Court of Quebec` THEN `s 493 three judges of the Court of Quebec`
    WHEN `s 525(7) an office that is none of those` THEN `s 493 an office that is none of those`

@ref s 525(7) (src:11754-11756)
GIVEN province IS A `Province or territory`
      `the order that the accused be detained in custody was made by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province of Quebec` IS A BOOLEAN
      office IS A `s 525(7) the office the person holds`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 525(7) the person is a judge for the purposes of this section in the Province of Quebec` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT province EQUALS Quebec THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In this section, judge, in the Province of Quebec" (for another province the definition of section 493 governs)
        IF `the order that the accused be detained in custody was made by a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the Province of Quebec`
            THEN `s 493 the person is a judge as defined in section 493` Quebec (`s 525(7)(a) the office as section 493 knows it` office)
        IF office EQUALS `s 525(7) a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province`
            OR office EQUALS `s 525(7) a judge of the Court of Quebec`
            OR office EQUALS `s 525(7) three judges of the Court of Quebec`
            THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in any other case, means a judge of the superior court of criminal jurisdiction of the province, a judge of the Court of Quebec or three judges of the Court of Quebec"

